WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.659 --> 00:00:14.503
morning was eventful at the March home, today being no different.

2
00:00:15.564 --> 00:00:17.966
Amy had overslept and was very cranky.

3
00:00:19.007 --> 00:00:22.770
Her hair, her most precious asset, looked limp and lifeless.

4
00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:26.093
"May I please be excused from school?

5
00:00:26.833 --> 00:00:32.690
I'm just not happy today," she whined, munching on a piece of dry bread that would have been

6
00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:35.593
warm and soft if she had gotten up in time to eat it.

7
00:00:35.613 --> 00:00:38.695
"Well, then we should all stay home.

8
00:00:39.336 --> 00:00:43.839
I'm not happy and neither is Meg," Jo shouted sarcastically from the foyer.

9
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:50.084
Late as usual, the two older girls were hastening to get out the door, but Jo couldn't find

10
00:00:50.164 --> 00:00:53.647
The Pirate's Enigma, a book she had borrowed from Aunt March.

11
00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:57.370
"Where could that stupid book be?"

12
00:00:57.731 --> 00:00:59.192
Jo yelled in frustration.

13
00:01:00.652 --> 00:01:03.354
"Jo! Mind your tongue and mind your temper!"

14
00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:06.516
Mother rebuked as she yanked at Amy's knots.

15
00:01:07.676 --> 00:01:10.898
"I'll look for the book," Beth offered in her timid manner.

16
00:01:10.918 --> 00:01:16.542
"Pray for me that Aunt March won't have an urge to hear that story read to her today.

17
00:01:17.522 --> 00:01:23.205
I'll just pretend to be deaf or have a sore throat if she does," Jo remarked, shoving her

18
00:01:23.326 --> 00:01:26.868
arms into her thick coat, and finally stepping outside the door.

19
00:01:28.404 --> 00:01:32.025
Blowing kisses at everyone, Meg and Jo began their trek to work.

20
00:01:33.285 --> 00:01:39.047
When Mother went to the window to wave at her girls, Amy reluctantly gathered her school books, got

21
00:01:39.067 --> 00:01:42.308
her lunch pail from Hannah, and dragged her feet to the foyer.

22
00:01:42.328 --> 00:01:48.490
"You're so lucky you can stay home all day," Amy said wistfully to Beth.

23
00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:54.511
At other times when Amy said this Beth would shake her head and say, "You're the lucky one.

24
00:01:55.271 --> 00:01:56.792
I wish I could go to school."

25
00:01:58.156 --> 00:02:04.239
Today, however, Beth did not say anything because inside she was feeling very lucky.

26
00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:09.262
Today she had something very special to look forward to.

27
00:02:10.443 --> 00:02:13.905
It seemed to take an eternity before everyone was finally gone.

28
00:02:14.945 --> 00:02:16.606
Beth was all by herself.

29
00:02:18.868 --> 00:02:25.331
The kitchen door of the March home faced the Laurence mansion, in particular the conservatory, where the object

30
00:02:25.371 --> 00:02:26.552
of Beth's desire was.

31
00:02:28.252 --> 00:02:33.355
Beth, however, had a major obstacle to overcome first: her fear.

32
00:02:33.375 --> 00:02:35.316
"What if Mr.

33
00:02:35.376 --> 00:02:38.417
Laurence suddenly walks into the conservatory?"

34
00:02:38.757 --> 00:02:39.718
she said to herself.

35
00:02:41.018 --> 00:02:44.420
"What if Laurie hears me play and thinks I'm horrible.

36
00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:47.341
Then what if he tells Jo?

37
00:02:48.942 --> 00:02:52.344
What if the door locks after I'm inside and I can't get out?"

38
00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:59.143
But no matter how many "what ifs" Beth could think of, her fear did not hold her back

39
00:02:59.203 --> 00:03:01.123
from the beautiful instrument inside.

40
00:03:02.204 --> 00:03:04.585
Taking a deep breath, she opened the kitchen door.

41
00:03:05.886 --> 00:03:11.228
Sticking her head out and checking to make sure no one was around, she took one brave step

42
00:03:11.268 --> 00:03:18.632
forward. Then, like a frightened field mouse, she scurried across the yard onto the stone pathway that led

43
00:03:18.692 --> 00:03:19.252
to the mansion.

44
00:03:20.128 --> 00:03:25.550
Pausing to cool her flushed cheeks, Beth felt like an intruder, as if she were entering a home

45
00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:26.210
not her own.

46
00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:33.392
Mr. Laurence, of course, had given his permission; yet, it was an odd sensation as Beth pushed open

47
00:03:33.412 --> 00:03:35.292
the glass doors to the conservatory.

48
00:03:36.813 --> 00:03:37.333
As Mr.

49
00:03:37.353 --> 00:03:44.175
Laurence had promised, the room was empty, and as before Beth caught her breath when her gaze fell

50
00:03:44.235 --> 00:03:45.875
upon the beautiful piano.

51
00:03:45.895 --> 00:03:49.276
"Hello. I'm Beth."

52
00:03:50.028 --> 00:03:54.311
The magnificence of the musical instrument impelled her to introduce herself.

53
00:03:55.471 --> 00:03:58.713
Giggling, she continued, "Mr.

54
00:03:58.793 --> 00:04:01.975
Laurence says I must come every day and look after you."

55
00:04:03.136 --> 00:04:04.857
She lightly stroked the keys.

56
00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:10.160
"He doesn't want you to get dusty or for your keys to get stuck."

57
00:04:11.441 --> 00:04:16.944
Even with Beth's amateur touch, she knew none of the polished keys ever got stuck.

58
00:04:18.828 --> 00:04:24.072
"But just between you and me," she leaned closer to the piano, as if she were whispering a

59
00:04:24.132 --> 00:04:28.895
secret, "I was hoping he would ask so I could come and play music on you."

60
00:04:29.856 --> 00:04:34.679
Pulling the stool out, Beth carefully sat down on the soft velvet cushion.

61
00:04:34.699 --> 00:04:36.561
"Oh, look!"

62
00:04:37.121 --> 00:04:40.563
Beth reached out to open an old leather book resting on the stand.

63
00:04:42.405 --> 00:04:46.688
Inside was a collection of sheet music, many of them songs that Beth knew.

64
00:04:48.072 --> 00:04:50.734
"You even prepared music for me to play.

65
00:04:51.455 --> 00:04:52.736
How kind you are!"

66
00:04:53.317 --> 00:04:55.899
Beth lovingly patted the top of the piano.

67
00:04:58.401 --> 00:05:04.926
After taking a moment to select a song, Beth clenched and unclenched her fists, as she'd seen pianists

68
00:05:04.966 --> 00:05:09.070
do. Then, ever so cautiously, she began to play.

69
00:05:10.911 --> 00:05:16.156
At first, the sounds were timid, like Beth, and unsure, lacking confidence and power.

70
00:05:17.416 --> 00:05:23.699
However, as she practiced and became more acquainted with her new friend, she felt comfortable enough to open

71
00:05:23.759 --> 00:05:24.399
her soul.

72
00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:30.681
Oblivious to the passing of time, Beth fell into a world of sound and harmony.

73
00:05:32.102 --> 00:05:35.844
True to her word, Beth visited the conservatory every day.

74
00:05:37.164 --> 00:05:42.866
Even though Hannah scolded her for not eating properly or practicing so long that her bones were stiff

75
00:05:42.926 --> 00:05:48.629
and numb, Beth felt that nothing could give her greater happiness than the time she spent playing music.

76
00:05:49.709 --> 00:05:56.072
Unknown to Beth, she already had a couple of secret admirers who also were finding joy and comfort

77
00:05:56.112 --> 00:05:56.832
in her melodies.

78
00:05:58.453 --> 00:06:04.135
One of them should have been paying closer attention to his lessons, but found himself straining his ears

79
00:06:04.235 --> 00:06:05.476
to hear Beth's music.

80
00:06:07.157 --> 00:06:13.259
After Laurie discovered he could hear Beth playing downstairs, he deliberately opened a window in the library in

81
00:06:13.299 --> 00:06:14.920
order to hear the music more clearly.

82
00:06:16.444 --> 00:06:18.225
"Must you keep that window open?

83
00:06:18.565 --> 00:06:20.286
It's freezing in here," Mr.

84
00:06:20.326 --> 00:06:22.127
Brookes complained to his young pupil.

85
00:06:23.388 --> 00:06:28.010
Mr. Brookes was not amused since the temperature outside was way below zero.

86
00:06:28.911 --> 00:06:35.414
The other admirer chose to sit in his study, lean back in his chair, and remember the time

87
00:06:35.474 --> 00:06:39.256
when his own little girl's music could be heard through those very walls.

88
00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:49.106
Since everyone was home on the weekends, Beth could not practice her beloved piano in the conservatory, but

89
00:06:49.166 --> 00:06:52.729
she continued to play the music in her mind wherever she was.

90
00:06:53.870 --> 00:07:00.756
One Saturday, after returning from the grocer's with Hannah, Beth found herself encircled by her sisters, all of

91
00:07:00.796 --> 00:07:02.438
them shouting with excitement at once.

92
00:07:02.458 --> 00:07:04.620
"You've got a gift, Beth!"

93
00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:05.681
screamed Amy.

94
00:07:05.701 --> 00:07:07.622
"A gift?"

95
00:07:08.063 --> 00:07:09.404
Beth asked, confused.

96
00:07:10.368 --> 00:07:11.069
"Come see it.

97
00:07:11.289 --> 00:07:14.771
Come!" Jo took Beth's arm and led her to the living room.

98
00:07:16.892 --> 00:07:23.157
As she stepped into the familiar room, Beth's eyes immediately went to the corner where something new stood.

99
00:07:24.257 --> 00:07:26.379
It was a beautiful solid oak piano.

100
00:07:26.399 --> 00:07:30.942
"Is this really for me?"

101
00:07:31.382 --> 00:07:33.403
she whispered, her voice trembling.

102
00:07:33.423 --> 00:07:36.005
"Look at this card, Beth!"

103
00:07:36.445 --> 00:07:38.487
Jo swung a white envelope in her face.

104
00:07:38.507 --> 00:07:40.188
"Read it!

105
00:07:40.492 --> 00:07:41.212
Hurry, Beth!"

106
00:07:41.452 --> 00:07:42.093
Amy pleaded.

107
00:07:42.113 --> 00:07:43.733
"I can't.

108
00:07:44.254 --> 00:07:45.254
I'm too nervous.

109
00:07:45.874 --> 00:07:48.055
Jo, can you read it for me, please?"

110
00:07:48.615 --> 00:07:49.156
asked Beth.

111
00:07:50.156 --> 00:07:53.477
Jo ripped the envelope open and read in a loud voice.

112
00:07:55.118 --> 00:08:00.520
My dearest Beth, I'm afraid you may not like what I am about to say.

113
00:08:01.881 --> 00:08:06.363
But I must confess that I have been listening to your beautiful music from my study.

114
00:08:07.523 --> 00:08:12.747
You may not realize it but your lovely melodies have brought much happiness back into my home.

115
00:08:14.308 --> 00:08:21.393
Therefore, as a token of my deepest appreciation, please accept this gift, which, at one time, belonged to

116
00:08:21.433 --> 00:08:22.453
my own daughter.

117
00:08:23.534 --> 00:08:27.937
May it bring much music and joy to your home and hearts, as it has done to mine.

118
00:08:28.958 --> 00:08:30.259
Your greatest admirer, Mr.
